  "aiOverview": {
    "content": "In the 2025 Final Four, No. 1 seed Duke lost to Houston after squandering a 14-point second-half lead, largely due to an offensive collapse where they managed only one field goal in the final 10:30. Houston’s intense full-court press, combined with critical Duke turnovers and missed free throws, fueled a 25-8 run by the Cougars to win 70-67. This video shows the final minutes of the game:48sBleacher ReportYouTube• Apr 6, 2025 48s Key reasons for the Duke collapse included: Offensive Stagnation: After leading 59-45 with 8:17 remaining, Duke's offense became \"absolute-zero cold,\" failing to execute effectively against Houston's pressure. Houston’s Defensive Pressure: Houston's top-ranked defense forced turnovers and created chaos, which led to high-pressure situations that Duke could not handle. Critical Misses and Fouls: Duke’s Tyrese Proctor missed the front end of a one-and-one free throw with the lead, and Cooper Flagg committed a costly over-the-back foul in the final 20 seconds, allowing Houston to take the lead. \"Toughness\" Factor: Houston coach Kelvin Sampson emphasized the team's resilience and physical play, enabling them to close the game on a 25-8 run. The loss was marked by intense pressure on Duke’s young team, resulting in turnovers on inbounds plays and inability to hold the lead, marking a significant \"choke\" in the final minutes.",
